It seems like the NetHack source code is supplying a "WinMain"
function, but your compiler is expecting a "main" function.

"WinMain" is the entry point for a Windows GUI program, and "main" is
the entry point for a Windows console program, or any ordinary C
program.

There are switches that must be supplied to the linker that tell it
what kind of .exe you want to compile, GUI or console. You can
probably run the compiler with a -? switch to find them.

